{"content":[{"c":["SCEPTER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Long staff with an ornamental head and other decorations used to represent royal authority; a shorter staff was used as a battle mace to symbolize royal military power. It is of more than passing interest that those two ideas are also conveyed by the Bible when the word “scepter” appears in a passage. The scepter of royal authority is referred to in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.49.10","r":"Gen.49.10","rawR":"Gen.49.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.49.10","value":"Gen.49.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 49:10"},", indicating that Judah’s descendants would exercise royal authority (so also in ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.45.6","r":"Ps.45.6","rawR":"Ps.45.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.45.6","value":"Ps.45.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 45:6"},", two times, and quoted in ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.1.8","r":"Heb.1.8","rawR":"Heb.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.1.8","value":"Heb.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 1:8"},"). Amos (",{"href":"?bref=Amos.1.5,8","r":"Amos.1.5,8","rawR":"Amos.1.5,8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.1.5,8","value":"Amos.1.5,8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 1:5, 8"},") refers to the royal authority of the kings of Syria and Philistia, and Zechariah (",{"href":"?bref=Zech.10.11","r":"Zech.10.11","rawR":"Zech.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.10.11","value":"Zech.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 10:11"},") refers to that of Egypt. King Ahasuerus held out this type of scepter to Esther (",{"href":"?bref=Esth.4.11","r":"Esth.4.11","rawR":"Esth.4.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.4.11","value":"Esth.4.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Est 4:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Esth.5.2","r":"Esth.5.2","rawR":"Esth.5.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.5.2","value":"Esth.5.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Esth.8.4","r":"Esth.8.4","rawR":"Esth.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.8.4","value":"Esth.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:4"},"). The scepter of royal military power is referred to in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.24.17","r":"Num.24.17","rawR":"Num.24.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.24.17","value":"Num.24.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 24:17"}," in reference to the coming messianic King. In ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.14.5","r":"Isa.14.5","rawR":"Isa.14.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.14.5","value":"Isa.14.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 14:5"}," it refers to the means by which Babylon exercised its oppressive military power, which was to be destroyed by God. ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.19.11,14","r":"Ezek.19.11,14","rawR":"Ezek.19.11,14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.19.11,14","value":"Ezek.19.11,14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezekiel 19:11, 14"}," uses “scepter” to refer to the authority, power, and dominion that Israel lost and was not able to regain."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Scepter","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Genesis 49:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.49.10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.49.10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.49.10"},{"anchorText":"Ps 45:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.45.6","rawQueryValue":"Ps.45.6","sourceRefExact":"Ps.45.6"},{"anchorText":"Heb 1:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Heb.1.8","rawQueryValue":"Heb.1.8","sourceRefExact":"Heb.1.8"},{"anchorText":"Am 1:5, 8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.1.5,8","rawQueryValue":"Amos.1.5,8","sourceRefExact":"Amos.1.5,8"},{"anchorText":"Zec 10:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zech.10.11","rawQueryValue":"Zech.10.11","sourceRefExact":"Zech.10.11"},{"anchorText":"Est 4:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.4.11","rawQueryValue":"Esth.4.11","sourceRefExact":"Esth.4.11"},{"anchorText":"5:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.5.2","rawQueryValue":"Esth.5.2","sourceRefExact":"Esth.5.2"},{"anchorText":"8:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.8.4","rawQueryValue":"Esth.8.4","sourceRefExact":"Esth.8.4"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 24:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.24.17","rawQueryValue":"Num.24.17","sourceRefExact":"Num.24.17"},{"anchorText":"Isaiah 14:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.14.5","rawQueryValue":"Isa.14.5","sourceRefExact":"Isa.14.5"},{"anchorText":"Ezekiel 19:11, 14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.19.11,14","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.19.11,14","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.19.11,14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"56e841c874c1f545c6bcd6d724b52723c384decb906e8e0d28ee0bd0654d01be","sourceItemName":"Scepter","sourceItemOrder":89,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Scepter","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Scepter","title":"Scepter","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}